<title>USA: U.S. Aug factory orders fell 1.9 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug factory orders fell 1.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce seasonally adjusted data on U.S. factory orders, shipments and unfilled orders.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:     Aug-Rev from    July--Rev from  June</p>
<p> New Orders		 -1.9		  1.7    1.8     -0.7</p>
<p> -Ex-Transportation     -1.1		  2.1    2.1     -0.6</p>
<p> -Ex-Defense		-2.1		  2.8    2.8     -1.2</p>
<p> NonDurables Orders     -0.4		  1.9    1.8     -1.2</p>
<p> Durables Orders	  -3.2   -3.1	 1.4    1.4     -0.2</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders -10.2  -10.1	 7.0    7.2     -4.6</p>
<p> -Ex-Aircraft, Parts    -5.0   -5.0	 3.7    3.9	2.6</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders     10.0    9.0     -40.7  -40.9     26.4</p>
<p> Durables NonDefense    -3.6   -3.5	 3.5    3.5     -1.2</p>
<p> Total Shipments	   0.1		  1.1    1.2     -0.8</p>
<p> Durables Shipments	0.3    0.3	 0.5    0.5     -0.3</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders  -0.3		  1.0    1.0	0.7</p>
<p> Unfilled Durables	-0.3   -0.3	 1.0    1.0	0.7</p>
<p>    In Blns of Dlrs:    Aug--Rev from   July--Rev from   June</p>
<p> New Orders	     311.15	     317.30  317.63   312.14</p>
<p> -Ex-Transportation   273.26	     276.18  276.04   270.38</p>
<p> -Ex-Defense	    305.86	     312.50  312.50   304.03</p>
<p> NonDurables Orders   144.35	     144.90  144.71   142.15</p>
<p> Durables Orders	166.80  167.01   172.40  172.40   169.99</p>
<p> NonDef. Cap Orders    41.26   41.37    45.94   46.01    42.92</p>
<p> -Ex-Aircraft, Parts   36.81   36.90    38.76   38.84    37.39</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders     5.29    5.22     4.81    4.79     8.11</p>
<p> Durables NonDefense  161.51  161.79   167.60  167.61   161.89</p>
<p> Total Shipments	312.64	     312.40	     308.85</p>
<p> Durables Shipments   168.24  168.24   167.77  167.70   166.90</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders  502.61	     504.11	     499.20</p>
<p> Unfilled Durables    478.59  478.87   480.03  480.10   475.40</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:     Aug-Rev from    July-Rev from   June</p>
<p> Primary Metals	   -2.6   -2.7	 1.6    1.6     -0.2</p>
<p> Industrial Machinery   -0.7   -0.7	 2.8    3.0	0.3</p>
<p> Electrical Equipment   -5.6   -5.6	 4.9    4.9	3.8</p>
<p> Transport Equipment    -7.9   -7.9	-1.5   -1.6     -1.3</p>
<p> Primary Metals	  15.39   15.38    15.80   15.81    15.55</p>
<p> Industrial Machinery  32.36   32.41    32.59   32.63    31.69</p>
<p> Electrical Equipment  26.49   26.51    28.07   28.08    26.77</p>
<p> Transport Equipment   37.89   37.87    41.13   41.10    41.76</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected a 1.2 percent decline in total factory orders for August.  </p>
<p>The department said the 1.9 percent drop in August factory orders was the largest monthly decrease since January 1993's drop of 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>The August inventories-to-shipments ratio was unchanged from July at 1.39. The department reported initial data on August orders for durable goods on September 26.</p>
